ake Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn8le10ob11re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le10ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn8le10ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn8le10ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: The nuts and seeds taste so good when they're roasted with some oil.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: You mean how you did them tonight?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: How many pain-killers did you take?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Well, my foot and hand don't hurt!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I was lucky that you came across that spice shop in Boston when you were out shopping.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Can you tell me where it is again?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh Sal! No more wine for you!"}, {"time": "19000", "image": "engenn8le10ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It was also very nice that I could get away with taking the day off. It's a rare treat.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: How did you manage to get the time?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I can take a day if I need it.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Nice. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Mmm. You can smell the cardamom and cinnamon stick in the rice. It's really fragrant too. Wash the rice carefully then boil it. Seeds can be roasted with a little oil. See, I remember."}, {"time": "41000", "image": "engenn8le10ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Vegetables should be cut away from you is what you need to recall!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Are you telling me to be more careful?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Exactly!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'm glad we had time to have lunch in Boston and catch up. I would go in for a few days away somewhere. Maybe we can get Peter to come round next weekend. We can go through the countryside maybe. I've got to face up to the fact that shopping, not cooking is my forte!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Thank goodness!"}]}}], "type": "audio"}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vanessa and the Cooking Accident", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "That Was a Close Call", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 10, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe  events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Inseparable Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use some inseparable phrasal verbs when you give opinions and others when you talk about social activities.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use phrasal verbs when you want to be less formal. They are very common in spoken English.<br/><br/>  Inseparable phrasal verbs cannot be separated. This means that you cannot put a noun between the verb and particle (preposition) as you can do with separable phrasal verbs.<br/><br/>  Example: Separable phrasal verb <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">to look up</span></span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Can you <span class=\"strong\">look up</span> that word?<br/> Can you <span class=\"strong\">look</span> that word <span class=\"strong\">up</span>?<br/> Can you <span class=\"strong\">look</span> it <span class=\"strong\">up</span>?</span><br/><br/>  Example: Inseparable phrasal verb <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">to go though</span></span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">went through</span> a dozen cook books.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">catch up<br/><br/>  go in for<br/><br/>  face up to <br/><br/>  go through<br/><br/>  come across  <br/><br/>come round<br/><br/>  get away with</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tell news<br/><br/>  enjoy; happily take<br/><br/>  realize<br/><br/>  from one side to the other<br/><br/>  find, by accident<br/><br/>  visit<br/><br/>  do without punishment\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I was lucky that you <span class=\"strong\">came across</span> that spice shop in Boston when you were out shopping.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm glad we had time to have lunch in Boston and <span class=\"strong\">catch up</span>.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I would <span class=\"strong\">go in for</span> a few days away somewhere. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Maybe we can get Peter to <span class=\"strong\">come round</span> next weekend.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We can <span class=\"strong\">go through</span> the countryside maybe.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've got to <span class=\"strong\">face up to</span> the fact that shopping, not cooking, is my forte!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It was also very nice that I could <span class=\"strong\">get away with</span> taking the day off.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Passive Modals and The Imperative to Talk About Food", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modal verbs to add meaning to other verbs. They come before the dictionary form (Infinitive without \u2018to') of the main verb.  Modal verbs can add meaning connected with certainty or obligation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use modal verbs in the passive voice. <br/> You use the passive voice when you want to focus on the receiver of the action, rather than the \u2018doer' of the action. <br/><br/>  Here is the structure of a passive sentence:<br/><br/>  Subject + to be + past participle<br/><br/>  For example:  <span class=\"italic\">Then some chives <span class=\"strong\">are sprinkled</span> on the salad!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can add a modal verb before the To be.<br/><br/>  Subject + modal + to be + past participle<br/><br/>  For example: <span class=\"italic\">Then some chives <span class=\"strong\">can be sprinkled</span> on the salad!</span><br/><br/>   Here the sentence now has an additional meaning of possibility, thanks to the modal <span class=\"strong\">can</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you are cooking, or talking about how to cook, you can also use the imperative.<br/> The imperative is used when giving directions.<br/> The subject \u2018you' is understood and left out.<br/><br/>  Example: <span class=\"italic\">Boil the vegetables</span>. = <span class=\"italic\">You boil the vegetables</span>.<br/><br/> By leaving out \u2018you' the statement becomes stronger and the focus is shifted to the verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can smell the cardamom and cinnamon stick in the rice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It's really fragrant too. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Wash the rice carefully, then boil it", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Seeds can be roasted with a little oil.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Vegetables should be cut away from you is what you need to recall!", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to get away with", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to succeed despite the difficulties", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It was also very nice that I could get away with taking the day off.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you need to review.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to recall", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to remember something or someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vegetables should be cut away from you is what you need to recall!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "cinnamon stick", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a common culinary spice that comes from a tree bark", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can smell the cardamom and cinnamon stick in the rice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "cardamom", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an aromatic seed coming from a plant of the same name ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can smell the cardamom in the rice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "fragrant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having a pleasant smell", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The rice is really fragrant too. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "thank goodness", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be pleased and happy about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Shopping, not cooking is my forte! <br/>         <span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Thank goodness! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to come round", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to visit, to stop in", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Maybe we can get Peter to come round next weekend.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to face up to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to accept that a difficult situation exists", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I've got to face up to the fact that shopping, not cooking is my forte!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Get in groups. Your group will debate if tipping is good.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Brainstorm reasons why tipping is good for society.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write three points as to why tipping is good.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Research online and find supporting details as to why.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Debate with another group who has the \"tipping is bad\" position.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Have the class decide who won the debate and give feedback.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I brainstorm ideas to support an opinion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I research my opinion and find details to support it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I debate with people with opposing views.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give feedback.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}